<title>GERMANY: SPRINGER, BERTELSMANN PLAN ONLINE SPORTS CHANNEL.</title>
<headline>SPRINGER, BERTELSMANN PLAN ONLINE SPORTS CHANNEL.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German media groups Axel Springer Verlag AG and Bertelsmann AG plan to launch an online sports channel this summer, Springer said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Both companies will own 50 percent of Sportkanal GmbH &amp; Co KG, which will make programmes which to be offered to subscribers of the America Online service in Germany.</p>
<p>Bertelsmann and America Online own 45 percent of AOL in Germany, while Springer owns the remaining 10 percent.</p>
<p>Springer said both partners saw good chances for specialised channels to succeed in new digital and interactive media. Springer will bring its resources from the Bild tabloid newspaper and Sport Bild magazine, while both will pool their expertise in television.</p>
<p>The venture will require the approval of German cartel authorities.</p>
